Experimental dish smoothing
===========================

These drivers preserve the smoothing experiments shared in Dropbox. They
are separate from the mesh import and preview routines. Smoothing is still
unresolved: no successful smoothed dish has been validated by this import.
The SurfSmooth3D dependency is not installed in the local project dependency
directory, and these drivers have not been run during the import.

Files
-----
run_smooth.m is the current fixed-CAD two-stage experiment for dish_fd023_m.
It retains the original adaptive/uniform mollifier choices, CAD oversampling,
Newton recovery, validity checks, and failure diagnostics.

launch.sh starts run_smooth under nohup. Its argument order is unchanged:
  launch.sh [adapt_sigma sigma_frac cad_order out_order rlam_override]

smooth_dish_rimfree.m preserves the earlier dish_fd021_m_rimfree experiment
with orders 4 and 8, rlam 10, and adaptive smoothing. These are historical
settings, not a validated recommendation for the thin closed shell.

dish_smoothing_paths.m resolves the input and dependency directories relative
to this code, rather than the working directory.

Inputs and dependencies
-----------------------
By default the MATLAB drivers read:
  <project>/data/dish/<stem>/<stem>_order4.go3
  <project>/data/dish/<stem>/<stem>_scaffold.gidmsh

Set DISH_MESH_ROOT to an absolute directory containing the stem directories
to use another mesh location. Meshes, scratch files, and generated results
under the project's data directory are ignored by Git.

SurfSmooth3D must provide matlab/setup_surfsmooth3d.m, the surfsmooth3d MATLAB
package, its compiled dependencies, and the two-stage/recovery APIs used in
these scripts. Set SURFSMOOTH3D_ROOT to its absolute repository directory.
Otherwise the default is <NRCCIE_DEPENDENCY_ROOT>/SurfSmooth3D, where
NRCCIE_DEPENDENCY_ROOT defaults to the parent of this project. No dependency
is downloaded or installed automatically.

Use
---
After installing the required smoother and making the mesh inputs available:

  addpath('/path/to/hirax_maxwell/src/dish/experimental')
  run_smooth(1,0.25,12,4)

The shell launcher can be called from any directory. Set MATLAB_BIN if MATLAB
is not on PATH, for example:

  MATLAB_BIN=/Applications/MATLAB_R2026a.app/bin/matlab \
    /path/to/hirax_maxwell/src/dish/experimental/launch.sh 1 0.25 12 4 50

The launcher validates all numerical arguments before constructing its MATLAB
batch command. An explicit rlam is appended to both the log and result tags,
so different rlam overrides do not reuse the same configuration path.

Results
-------
run_smooth writes into <mesh-root>/<stem>/smooth/<configuration>/, including
the manifest, run log, and any generated go3 or failure/recovery diagnostics.
The historical driver writes into <mesh-root>/<stem>/smooth/.

Each invocation creates a unique scratch directory under smooth/work/ and
does not delete another run's scratch directory. Existing result files for
the same configuration may be replaced; run duplicate configurations in
separate mesh roots if they must be retained. Scratch diagnostics are left
available for inspection. A status of "solved" records that the smoother
returned; inspect the separate validity result before accepting a mesh.

Provenance
----------
Imported from Dropbox/hirax/geometry/dish/mesh/out:
  dish_fd023_m/run_smooth.m
  dish_fd023_m/launch.sh
  dish_fd021_m_rimfree/smooth/smooth_dish_rimfree.m

The numerical algorithms and original experimental comments were preserved.
Import changes are path configuration, input checks, independent scratch
directories, explicit rlam tags, and portable shell launching.
